# 25. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

Treat security as a core implementation requirement.

* Reuse the existing Supabase authentication system.
* Reuse existing admin authorization logic.
* Enforce Row Level Security.
* Never expose the Supabase service-role key in frontend code.
* Never place privileged secrets in Vite variables exposed to the browser.
* Validate all customer actions on the server.
* Validate admin actions on the server.
* Never trust frontend product prices, discounts, reward status, customer IDs, or order totals.
* Use cryptographically secure tokens.
* Store sensitive tokens securely, using hashes where appropriate.
* Rate-limit verification-code attempts.
* Avoid leaking whether another customer's reward exists.
* Prevent duplicate orders with idempotency.
* Use atomic transactions for reward redemption, stock reservation, and order creation.
* Add appropriate audit logs.
* Avoid storing verification codes or sensitive tokens in logs.
* Ensure link previews do not redeem rewards.
* Never automatically send WhatsApp messages unless a legitimate approved integration has been configured.
* Never fake payment success.
* Never invent successful test results.

If backend functions or database procedures are required, implement them using the existing project's supported backend architecture.

